{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0e00e645b8daf3e7c0235365253d43f81c750ac183df914a5e2d45b127b5df88"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"agent send supports --stdin for piped input, --wait to block until a response, --timeout in milliseconds, --json structured output, and --group for sending to saved agent groups."},{"claim_ids":["clm_627d829ba3f32cd5f2fb1ee8f98f3a4b50beeca60147ae46eb910dba740e38dc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A single .ai-devkit.json config reconciles setup across supported agents, and init writes per-agent directories, skills, MCP settings, and docs/ai phase folders."},{"claim_ids":["clm_65f10b9848277131091a6d0d75cd9fbe28c47d48626832cfab51791beb87651f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A channel command bridges running agent sessions to external channels such as Telegram and Slack, with named configs, daemon mode, stop/status commands, and authorization state reporting."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7b60b6b7cdda99d008059e9a9f24816afc8d1666b19fa3be8340a70024a4f61c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Nine built-in skills are documented, anchored by dev-lifecycle, plus verify, tdd, structured-debug, memory, dev-commit, document-code, simplify-implementation, and technical-writer."},{"claim_ids":["clm_82ca6c942a0816f17fd9de53073b1412977e5a4a343dc7888014d785c6db15fc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors clone the repo, run npm install and npm run build, and contributing guidance lives in CONTRIBUTING.md."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9a8f9904663487a5be3c373f07749e1507fc0fae6d7139369f45947f0a87980f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Memory stores project decisions, conventions, and fixes in a local SQLite file, exposed through MCP and CLI, with store and search commands and opt-in hybrid semantic search."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b8d8bdea9e2e7023abc49bdc9d9af76e740d6d08a8d8cca6d72fededf2a7dcb4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI exposes agent subcommands including agent list, agent detail, agent console, agent send, agent start, and agent rename; agent kill is documented as a console command with confirmation and tmux cleanup."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d2535d283b54d38cbf9fe5aec52a1bdc128aeafca0a14b5e6e31ebec046e729d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The verify skill blocks completion claims without fresh test or build evidence, and dev-commit checks diffs, stages explicit paths, validates, and reports the SHA/status."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e3e02f21aa765804791976a0bc11fa9767c2548d851540defd5921545cc77c9e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool targets developers running multiple AI coding agents who lack a shared control surface, maintain separate per-tool config files, and have no easy way to message running sessions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fbce3145a3f79cf234902a7c2cb97925325c1fa916babc919920994f3e4fb541"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README states the tool is not a smarter LLM, not a replacement for the coding agents it coordinates, and not a hosted service; it runs locally with no telemetry."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0e00e645b8daf3e7c0235365253d43f81c750ac183df914a5e2d45b127b5df88","clm_627d829ba3f32cd5f2fb1ee8f98f3a4b50beeca60147ae46eb910dba740e38dc","clm_65f10b9848277131091a6d0d75cd9fbe28c47d48626832cfab51791beb87651f","clm_7b60b6b7cdda99d008059e9a9f24816afc8d1666b19fa3be8340a70024a4f61c","clm_82ca6c942a0816f17fd9de53073b1412977e5a4a343dc7888014d785c6db15fc","clm_9a8f9904663487a5be3c373f07749e1507fc0fae6d7139369f45947f0a87980f","clm_b8d8bdea9e2e7023abc49bdc9d9af76e740d6d08a8d8cca6d72fededf2a7dcb4","clm_d2535d283b54d38cbf9fe5aec52a1bdc128aeafca0a14b5e6e31ebec046e729d","clm_e3e02f21aa765804791976a0bc11fa9767c2548d851540defd5921545cc77c9e","clm_fbce3145a3f79cf234902a7c2cb97925325c1fa916babc919920994f3e4fb541"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:42:05Z","created_by_operation":"op_9dfeee4b6cce483d91a9a38c69e9e7cf","id":"pg_d99799b0c22b5bee8953481165ac37e8","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/codeaholicguy-ai-devkit-readme-md-1a3a0024eb3b-481165ac37